---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const species = await getCollection("species");
const sites = await getCollection("sites");
const archived = species[0]?.data.source.archived ?? "2026";
---

<Layout title="About BirdWeb" description="What BirdWeb is, where its data comes from, and how this edition was rebuilt.">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand">About BirdWeb</h1>

  <div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-black/80">
    <p>
      BirdWeb is Birds Connect Seattle's guide to the birds of Washington state. It holds
      {species.length} species accounts, {sites.length} birding site descriptions, and
      abundance records for all ten of Washington's ecoregions, month by month — written
      and maintained by BCS volunteers since 1999.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand pt-2">Reading the abundance data</h2>
    <p>
      For every species, BirdWeb records how likely you are to encounter it in each
      ecoregion in each month of the year, on a five-point scale:
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-1.5 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-sage">
      <li><strong>Common</strong> — found in moderate to large numbers, and easily found in suitable habitat.</li>
      <li><strong>Fairly common</strong> — found in small to moderate numbers, and usually easy to find.</li>
      <li><strong>Uncommon</strong> — present but not certain to be seen, even in suitable habitat.</li>
      <li><strong>Rare</strong> — occurs annually in very small numbers; not to be expected on any given day.</li>
      <li><strong>Irregular</strong> — numbers vary widely from year to year; may be absent entirely in some years.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A blank means the species has not been recorded there in that month. These are
      judgements by experienced Washington field ornithologists, not survey counts.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand pt-2">About this edition</h2>
    <p>
      The original BirdWeb ran from 2002 until this rebuild. Its source code and database
      were lost, and the server that hosted it could no longer be administered, so the
      content was recovered directly from the live site in {archived} and rebuilt as a
      static site that works on a phone as well as a desktop.
    </p>
    <p>
      The accounts are reproduced as their authors wrote them. Where a bird's name or
      classification has changed since publication, the current name is shown and the
      original is noted on the page rather than the text being rewritten — the accounts are
      a record of what BCS's volunteers knew and published, and that is worth preserving
      alongside current taxonomy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand pt-2">Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Found an error, or have a photograph to contribute? Write to
      <a href="mailto:info@birdsconnectsea.org?subject=BirdWeb%20feedback" class="text-brand underline decoration-sage underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-brand">info@birdsconnectsea.org</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <a href={`${base}credits/`} class="rounded-full bg-brand text-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-brand-dark transition">Credits</a>
    <a href="https://birdsconnectsea.org/donate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full bg-pop text-brand px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold hover:brightness-95 transition">Support BCS</a>
  </div>
</Layout>
